==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|s|ä}}

===Etymology 1===
Baltic-Finnic cognates of the same meaning are deemed certain and include eg. Karelian {{term|seä||lang=krl}}, Votic {{term|sää|lang=vot}}, Veps {{term|sä|lang=vep}}. Probably inherited from {{etyl|fiu-pro|fi}} {{term/t|fiu-pro|*säŋi||air}}, also reflected in Hungarian {{term|ég||sky|lang=hu}} and Komi-Zyrian {{term|сынӧд||warm air|tr=synöd|lang=kv}}.

====Noun====
{{head|fi|noun}}

# [[weather]]
#:* [[hyvä]]llä ''säällä'' = on good ''weather''
#:* [[huono]]lla ''säällä'' = on bad ''weather''

=====Declension=====
{{fi-decl-maa|sä|ä|ä}}

